</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Corrupt rhyme rate (%) when all layers are patched simultaneously, with Wilson 95% CIs. All cells use <math id="A4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}100</annotation></semantics></math> (5 prompt pairs <math id="A4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times\ N{=}20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.682em">×</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times\ N{=}20</annotation></semantics></math>). Gemma-3-27B is the only model whose newline-patching CI does not overlap zero, separated by a wide margin from every other model.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Per-Layer Results: All Models</h3>

<figure id="A4.F14" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07984v1/media/results-patching/patching_summary_bars-updated.png" id="A4.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/162;" width="476" height="162" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F14.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 14</span>: </span><span id="A4.F14.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Peak corrupt rhyme rate (maximum across all layers) for the last word token and newline (<math id="A4.F14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math>) at each model size. Black error bars are 95% cluster bootstrap CIs over prompt pairs (5 pairs per model). Gemma-3-27B is the only model whose newline CI is clearly separated from zero (0.63 [0.48, 0.78]); every other model has a newline CI upper bound <math id="A4.F14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 0.21" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.21</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 0.21</annotation></semantics></math> regardless of scale, while last-word patching is broadly effective from <math id="A4.F14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math>3B parameters onward in every family.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07984v1/media/results-patching/appendix_patching_Qwen3_small-updated.png" id="A4.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/313;" width="476" height="313" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F15.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 15</span>: </span><span id="A4.F15.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Per-layer activation patching, Qwen3 0.6B–4B. Black bars are 95% cluster bootstrap CIs (5 pairs <math id="A4.F15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times\ N{=}20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.682em">×</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times\ N{=}20</annotation></semantics></math>). Last-word patching becomes effective only from 4B (peak 0.48 [0.25, 0.72]); 0.6B and 1.7B have peak CIs that nearly span zero. Newline (<math id="A4.F15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math>) patching is at noise across all sizes (peak CI upper bounds <math id="A4.F15.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 0.21" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.21</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 0.21</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F16" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07984v1/media/results-patching/appendix_patching_Qwen3_large-updated.png" id="A4.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/313;" width="476" height="313" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F16.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 16</span>: </span><span id="A4.F16.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Per-layer activation patching, Qwen3 8B–32B. Black bars are 95% cluster bootstrap CIs. Last-word peaks rise smoothly with scale (8B 0.54 [0.35, 0.72]; 14B 0.73 [0.46, 0.97]; 32B 0.74 [0.55, 0.93]). Newline patching remains at noise across all three sizes (CI upper bounds <math id="A4.F16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 0.21" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.21</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 0.21</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F17" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07984v1/media/results-patching/appendix_patching_Gemma3-updated.png" id="A4.F17.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/418;" width="476" height="418" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F17.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 17</span>: </span><span id="A4.F17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Per-layer activation patching, Gemma-3 1B–27B. Black bars are 95% cluster bootstrap CIs. The newline (<math id="A4.F17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math>) channel is silent at every size below 27B (peak CI [0.00, 0.00] for 4B and 12B), and only emerges at 27B with peak 0.63 [0.48, 0.78] at L33. Last-word (<math id="A4.F17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=-2</annotation></semantics></math>) patching is effective from 1B onward.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A4.F18" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07984v1/media/results-patching/appendix_patching_Llama3-updated.png" id="A4.F18.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/418;" width="476" height="418" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F18.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 18</span>: </span><span id="A4.F18.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Per-layer activation patching, Llama-3 1B–70B. Black bars are 95% cluster bootstrap CIs. Last-word peaks are high from 3B onward (3B 0.91 [0.86, 0.96]; 8B 0.85 [0.73, 0.97]; 70B 0.86 [0.74, 0.96]); 1B is lower (peak 0.66 [0.56, 0.75]). Newline patching is at noise across all four sizes (CI upper bounds <math id="A4.F18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 0.09" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.09</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 0.09</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
